From 9c1f2e3a4b5d6f708192a3b4c5d6e7f8091a2b3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-9 remaining UART byte planes

Register the four batch-9 Units that have an executable UART path as
byte-layer fixture responders, on the reconciled canonical chain. Base is the
30-layer chain through 0149 (canonical 75f1d24 plus 0120-0149); this is the
31st layer after 0120 and it applies at the chain end. The batch-7 evidence fix
is 0150 and remains a separate parallel layer pending reconciliation; this
patch does not touch its catm/lorawan-cn470 code paths.

- lorawan-as923 (U184-AS923) and lorawan-eu868 (U184-EU868): reuse the existing
  UART TX-capture + idle fixture responder for the AT byte layer. The frozen
  unit/lorawan.py still wraps the ASR650x LoRaWAN_470 class while the products
  are STM32WLE5/RAK3172; there is no AS923 subclass and the EU868 wrapper does
  not use LoRaWAN_868. Only TX/RX hex, frames-sent and frames-injected are
  exposed. OTAA/ABP/Join, band masks and RF/antenna/regulatory behavior are NOT
  modeled.
- audioplayer (U197): UART 9600 byte capture and deterministic idle fixture
  responses only. There is no public Unit AudioPlayer driver and the N9301
  command/status table is not readable, so no command decode/audio claim.
- fingerprint2 (U203): UART 115200 byte capture and idle fixture responses
  only. A-K323CP has no public Unit driver/frame table and is a different chip
  from batch-6 finger (FPC1020A), so no frame/version/biometric claim.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 m5cores3, no guest firmware) attaches all four Unit ids,
lists responses-hex/tx-hex/frames-sent/frames-injected, sets responses-hex and
verifies the fixture round-trip property storage. The smoke is not a functional
PASS and no guest/Device Service evidence is recorded; all four catalog/profile
entries stay planned. The five remaining batch-9 Units (cardkb2, 8servos2-i2c,
bmm350, ina226-10a, rollercan) are registered as planned contracts only, with no
QEMU model and no guessed registers.
